# Idle Process Metric Feature — Diff Summary

Below is a summary of the changes across each file (paraphrased with short verbatim snippets under 125 characters where needed for accuracy). This is Apache-licensed (ASL 2.0) code.

## Property.java
Two new enum properties added:
- **`GENERAL_IDLE_PROCESS_INTERVAL`** — key `"general.metrics.process.idle"`, default `"5m"`, type `TIMEDURATION`, version `"4.0.0"`. Description: `"Amount of time a process must be idle before the accumulo.server.idle metric is incremented."`
- **`GENERAL_MICROMETER_USER_TAGS`** — key `"general.micrometer.user.tags"`, default empty, type `STRING`, version `"4.0.0"`. Allows comma-separated tags like `tag1=value1,tag2=value2`.

## MetricsProducer.java
New constant added after `METRICS_LOW_MEMORY`:
```java
String METRICS_SERVER_IDLE = "accumulo.server.idle";
```

## MetricsUtil.java
- The `configure`/init caller now passes `conf.get(Property.GENERAL_MICROMETER_USER_TAGS)`.
- `initializeMetrics(...)` signature gained a trailing `String userTags` parameter.
- New parsing block: if `userTags` is non-empty, split on `","`, then split each on `"="`; if `tagParts.length == 2`, add `Tag.of(tagParts[0], tagParts[1])`, else log a warning about a malformed tag.

## AbstractServer.java
New imported `java.util.function.Supplier`. New fields:
```java
protected final long idleReportingPeriodNanos;
private volatile long idlePeriodStartNanos = 0L;
```
Constructor sets `idleReportingPeriodNanos` via `TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS.toNanos(...)` from `GENERAL_IDLE_PROCESS_INTERVAL`. New method:
```java
protected void idleProcessCheck(Supplier<Boolean> idleCondition) {
  boolean idle = idleCondition.get();
  if (!idle || idleReportingPeriodNanos == 0) {
    idlePeriodStartNanos = 0;
  } else if (idlePeriodStartNanos == 0) {
    idlePeriodStartNanos = System.nanoTime();
  } else if ((System.nanoTime() - idlePeriodStartNanos) > idleReportingPeriodNanos) {
    processMetrics.incrementIdleCounter();
    idlePeriodStartNanos = 0;
  } else {
    // idleStartPeriod is non-zero, but we have not hit the idleStopPeriod yet
  }
}
```

## ProcessMetrics.java
- Removed `java.util.List` import; added `MetricsUtil`, `io.micrometer.core.instrument.Counter`.
- New field `private Counter idleCounter;`
- In `registerMetrics(MeterRegistry registry)`: low-memory gauge now uses `MetricsUtil.getCommonTags()`, and:
```java
idleCounter = registry.counter(METRICS_SERVER_IDLE, MetricsUtil.getCommonTags());
```
- New method:
```java
public void incrementIdleCounter() {
  if (idleCounter != null) {
    idleCounter.increment();
  }
}
```

## Compactor.java
Added `AtomicLong` import. In the run loop, `final AtomicLong timeSinceLastCompletion = new AtomicLong(0L);` and an `idleProcessCheck(...)` call whose condition returns true if never started a compaction (`== 0`) or if the elapsed nanos since last completion exceeds `idleReportingPeriodNanos`. In the `finally` block: `timeSinceLastCompletion.set(System.nanoTime());`

## ScanServer.java
Inside the server loop (after the 1-second sleep):
```java
idleProcessCheck(() -> {
  return sessionManager.getActiveScans().isEmpty()
      && tabletMetadataCache.estimatedSize() == 0;
});
```

## TabletServer.java
Added `idleProcessCheck(() -> getOnlineTablets().isEmpty());` at three points: at the top of the `while (!serverStopRequested)` loop, inside the inner `while (mm == null && !serverStopRequested)` polling loop, and after the immediate `managerMessages.poll()` retrieval. Also a comment typo fix (`sever` → `server`).

## Test Changes
- **`IdleProcessMetricsIT.java`** (new): starts servers in an `IDLE_PROCESS_TEST` resource group with `GENERAL_IDLE_PROCESS_INTERVAL` set to `"10s"`, waits 20s, then scans StatsD lines starting with `METRICS_SERVER_IDLE`, checking the `process.name` tag equals `tserver`, `sserver`, or `compactor`.
